ional midwife has a  certificate through an  organization like the north american  registry of midwives  executive director ida dara says that's  earned by passing a test and  working under the supervision of an  experienced midwife for prenatal visits  newborn exams and at least 55  births what would you say to critics who  say  they're essentially providing medical  care  without medical training i would say  they're providing midwifery care  with midwifery training 100 deliveries  was the number of deliveries i did my  first  month of my four years of residency  first  month dr stacy mchale is an ovgyn in las  vegas and the president-elect of the  clark county medical society  she says she supports a collaboration  between a midwife  and physician from the start the  differences in the levels of training  are very  are very noticeable and those levels of  training  and the need to have expertise and the  need to have someone to provide  backup if there is an emergency  situation is  crucial for the health of our mothers in  nevada i have seen many of the  complications that can happen  with deliveries even those that we  anticipate are going to be  normal and having home birth  midwives makes me very anxious what  about those  rare emergencies is it worth taking a  chance  nobody looks at their own pregnancy as  taking a chance i mean that's why you're  getting regular prenatal care and  assessment  so that you have a clue if anything is  uh  potentially problematic but could  something really  uh surprising come up it can come up and  that's why you need to address  what you will do if you have problems  like that right now nevada has no  oversight of any midwives through senate  bill 271  senator hammond is proposing the  creation of a board of certified  professional midwives  licensing for cpms and permits for  apprentices  with oversight there would be  regulations and disciplinary action  would be possible  while assembly bill 387 is similar  it states if a